---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="security-model" title="Security & permission model">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Optional 06B</p>
      <h1>Security & permission model.</h1>
      <p>
        This is optional for getting started, but essential once agents can touch
        real systems. The core principle is simple: least privilege by default,
        explicit approval for risky actions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="signal-panel signal-panel--definitions" style="margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <div>
        <article>
          <span>Principle</span>
          <strong>Least privilege</strong>
          <p>Expose only the minimum tools and scopes needed for the current workflow.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Control</span>
          <strong>Policy gates</strong>
          <p>Require confirmation for irreversible, high-cost, or externally visible actions.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Visibility</span>
          <strong>Audit trail</strong>
          <p>Log who requested what, which tool executed, and what side effects occurred.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Permission layers</p>
      <h2>Design permissions as a stack, not a single switch.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mini-diagram react-diagram" aria-label="Permission layers flow diagram" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 160" role="img">
        <defs>
          <marker id="react-arrow" markerHeight="8" markerWidth="8" orient="auto" refX="7" refY="4">
            <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z"></path>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <g class="react-links">
          <path d="M 120 80 H 140" marker-end="url(#react-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 244 80 H 264" marker-end="url(#react-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 368 80 H 388" marker-end="url(#react-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 492 80 H 512" marker-end="url(#react-arrow)"></path>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="16" y="58" width="104" height="44" rx="22"></rect>
          <text x="68" y="84">Identity</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="140" y="58" width="104" height="44" rx="22"></rect>
          <text x="192" y="84">Tool</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-planner">
          <rect x="264" y="58" width="104" height="44" rx="22"></rect>
          <text x="316" y="84">Data</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-critic">
          <rect x="388" y="58" width="104" height="44" rx="22"></rect>
          <text x="440" y="84">Action</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-done">
          <rect x="512" y="58" width="104" height="44" rx="22"></rect>
          <text x="564" y="84">Review</text>
        </g>
        <text class="loop-caption" x="316" y="136">defense in depth across the agent stack</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <ul class="timeline-list">
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Identity layer</strong>
          <p>Bind actions to user/service identity with scoped credentials and short-lived tokens.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Tool layer</strong>
          <p>Allowlist tools per workflow and deny tools that are not explicitly required.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Data layer</strong>
          <p>Segment sensitive data, redact by default, and enforce retrieval access boundaries.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">04</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Action layer</strong>
          <p>Gate destructive operations (write/delete/send/publish) behind approval checks.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">05</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Review layer</strong>
          <p>Retain trace artifacts for post-incident analysis, compliance, and policy iteration.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="warning-note">
      <strong>Caution:</strong> Security failures in agent systems are usually permission-design failures.
      Keep capabilities narrow, approvals explicit, and logs complete.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
